@startuml
title Two-phase commit: what it does, and where it blocks
participant "Coordinator" as C
participant "Order\ndatabase" as O
participant "Inventory\ndatabase" as I
participant "Payment\ndatabase" as P

== phase 1: prepare ==
C -> O : prepare
O --> C : yes
C -> I : prepare
I --> C : yes
C -> P : prepare
P --> C : yes
note over O, P : each participant has promised to commit:\nit holds its locks until told what to do

== phase 2: commit ==
C -> O : commit
C -> I : commit
note over C #FFCDD2 : the coordinator stops here
note over P #FFF8E1 : in doubt: prepared, not told.\nIt cannot commit, cannot roll back,\nand keeps its locks until\nthe coordinator comes back
@enduml
